# Provenance and licence record for every artifact bundled into the image (artifacts/).
# One row per artifact; pipe-delimited; a row's path is the path inside artifacts/ and must
# match MANIFEST.sha256 exactly (tests/test_provenance_manifest.sh enforces this and that
# no field is empty). Rows whose path starts with "embedded:" describe a third-party
# component linked into a listed artifact; they have no file of their own. Rows whose path
# starts with "image-package:" describe one Alpine package installed in the container image
# (name and version as the image's apk database records them); rows starting with
# "image-component:" describe software in the image that is not an apk package, the base
# image itself, and the add-on's own files. Those rows have no file in artifacts/ and a
# sha256 of "not-applicable" unless a checksum is stated in the notes, or unless the field holds a value measured from the image: the sha256 of one file, or a tree digest (the sha256 of the byte-wise path-sorted list of `sha256sum` lines of the regular files under a stated path set; the row notes define the path set; symlinks and directories are not covered). Image rows were
# generated from the 0.4.0-rc.1 image (tools/generate_sbom.sh) and re-measured against the image rebuilt on 2026-10-31 on the refreshed base image; the licence of an
# apk package is the package metadata value, checked against the package build file (apkbuild-confirmed).
# The four Python rows (pyc, python3, python3-pyc, python3-pycache-pyc0) were regenerated after
# the Python pin changed to 3.12.16-r0 (the previous revision is no longer served by the package
# index). On 2026-10-31 the base image was refreshed (Alpine 3.23.7): the 15 apk rows whose package
# changed (version, aports commit, apk database checksum), the base-image row, the CA bundle row and
# the image identity quoted in the rows were re-measured from the rebuilt image; the generator's
# cross-check reports every row and component as matching.
# Completeness of the image rows: every file in the image that no apk package owns is accounted
# for by a row below: the s6-overlay tree and its symlinks (the s6 family rows), tempio, bashio,
# jemalloc (image-component:jemalloc, built from source by the base image and not an apk package),
# the base image configuration file /etc/pip.conf (image-component:base-image-config), and the
# add-on's own files. This was established by listing the files of the 0.4.0-rc.1 image that the
# apk database does not own, on 2026-10-30. tests/test_sbom_completeness.sh checks the form of
# this record; tools/generate_sbom.sh checks it against a built image and reports any image
# package, non-apk component or bundled artifact that has no row, and any row with no SBOM entry.
#
# licence_check:  confirmed          the licence text of the pinned source was read from that exact ref
#                 from-bundle-record recorded when the artifact was built; not re-read since
#                 apkbuild-confirmed the license equals the license= line of the package build file (APKBUILD)
#                                    at the recorded aports commit; upstream license files were not read
#                 unverified         not yet checked
# redistribution: approved           redistribution of the component is approved, with its existing license and
#                                    notices retained; the license texts are in LICENSES/ and third-party-notices/.
#                                    The approval does not change any license and is not a legal conclusion
#
# path | sha256 | component | source | source_ref | licence | licence_text | licence_check | redistribution | notes
./morse.ko | bafaafb281912c28f22d746032dce1d0cef5d40e4d651e4d6fc752c22f324c7a | Morse Micro driver (morse) | https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse_driver | 4ce0a0272f8ac8e2fa58eea8ff08116e493399de | GPL-2.0-only | LICENSE at the repository root (GNU GPL version 2) | confirmed | approved | Rebuilt 2026-10-28 for Home Assistant OS 18.4 (kernel 6.18.58-haos, vermagic 6.18.58-haos SMP preempt mod_unload aarch64) with source-offer/build-modules.sh in path-independent mode (GNU build-id 058f9e62fe57bbfc28d021e63357f63e224feba5, srcversion C601E85123B2E7F4B6A44FE, 28634680 bytes); four builds at different locations gave identical bytes. It replaces the 6.18.52 build and will not load on a different kernel. Build inputs: corresponding_source.psv (kernel 6.18.58, Operating System tag 18.4, nine patches, derived configuration, Buildroot commit d2b75e05; the 18.4 image itself was built with -g30c038aa). Not byte-identical to the build that made the 18.4 kernel and its host modules, and loaded on one Green (Home Assistant OS 18.4, kernel 6.18.58-haos) in a live test on 2026-10-30. Morse Micro treats this module as GPL-2.0-only. The module's own MODULE_LICENSE tag, read from the binary, is 'Dual BSD/GPL'; correcting that tag is a matter for the upstream Morse Micro software team, and the binary is not changed here. Corresponding source: see SOURCE-OFFER.md.
./dot11ah.ko | 73535f72576a466ce1f14e1a7449e3c60b16182c5b494c8eb5437fce0b2655af | Morse Micro driver (dot11ah regulatory/S1G module) | https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse_driver | 4ce0a0272f8ac8e2fa58eea8ff08116e493399de | GPL-2.0-only | LICENSE at the repository root (GNU GPL version 2) | confirmed | approved | Rebuilt 2026-10-28 from the same commit and for the same kernel (6.18.58-haos) as morse.ko, same build inputs (GNU build-id e3a7b0d544a0518254e305d97e3665dc159c40f2, srcversion 3B02991D4DB75E404FAEB63, 133440 bytes); replaces the 6.18.52 build; loaded on one Home Assistant Green (Home Assistant OS 18.4) in live tests on 2026-10-30 and 2026-10-31; loaded with channelization_scheme=2 (the IEEE 802.11-2024 scheme). Inventory item: the module's own MODULE_LICENSE tag, read from the binary, is 'Dual BSD/GPL'.
./hostapd_s1g | 6904fd491a9395c90723cbbfaa8193bf9f68897c7bf7b2a7bf7165e4fa4a5e21 | hostapd (Morse Micro S1G fork), statically linked | https://github.com/MorseMicro/hostap | e7309b438eaec4b82f2db29e8ef7beaca3ca52c6 | BSD-3-Clause AND ISC (repository-level license BSD-3-Clause; src/utils/radiotap.c, which is compiled in, is dual GPL-2.0 or ISC and is used under ISC; the radiotap and nl80211 header files are ISC) | COPYING and README at the repository root; copies are in third-party-notices/ | confirmed | approved | Tag mm8108-2.1.0, the same release as the bundled driver and firmware. COPYING and README read at the pinned ref; both are identical to those of the earlier 1.17.9 ref, and the BSD text itself is in the README (copyright 2002-2024 Jouni Malinen and contributors). Of the 251 source and header files in the compiled set (derived with make -n on a native compiler, not the cross toolchain), 244 carry the standard BSD wording; src/common/morse/morse_commands.h carries only a copyright line (Copyright 2025-2026 Morse Micro) and is covered by the repository-level BSD-3-Clause; src/utils/morse.c and morse.h carry the BSD pointer; ieee802_11_vht.c uses older BSD wording; src/utils/radiotap.c is dual GPL-2.0 or ISC and is used under ISC (the ISC text is in radiotap.h, copied to third-party-notices/). No GPL-only or other copyleft file is in the compiled set. Statically links OpenSSL (see the embedded row). Built with the vendor defconfig plus CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MORSE=y and CONFIG_MORSE_5GHZ_MAPPED=y, DPP, DPP2, DPP3 and OWE disabled, and -Wno-error=unused-variable because this tag fails its own -Werror build at ap_config.c:849 (an unused variable in a configuration that does not enable WPS); the flag changes no behavior. It talks to the driver over nl80211 vendor commands and runs no helper program. The stripped executables ran in a bounded smoke test on one Home Assistant Green on 2026-10-31. Shipped stripped with the build toolchain's own strip and free of build-machine path strings (the home directory, user name, workspace, temporary and toolchain build directories); rebuilt byte for byte from different directories by source-offer/build-hostapd.sh. Compared with the earlier unstripped build, all sections have the same sizes and the code is identical except for address offsets that moved with the compiled-in OpenSSL directory names, which are now /usr/local/ssl, /usr/local/lib/engines-3 and /usr/local/lib/ossl-modules. The stripped file itself ran in the bounded smoke test on one Home Assistant Green on 2026-10-31.
./hostapd_cli_s1g | 8e8e04917aa6156697db66cbe3c6cd78a39b19a65a3b387fe615234f559341dd | hostapd control client (Morse Micro S1G fork) | https://github.com/MorseMicro/hostap | e7309b438eaec4b82f2db29e8ef7beaca3ca52c6 | BSD-3-Clause AND ISC (as hostapd_s1g) | COPYING and README at the repository root; copies are in third-party-notices/ | confirmed | approved | Tag mm8108-2.1.0; built in the same step as hostapd_s1g with the same flags. Run by path by the manager to read the access point's status and station list. Shipped stripped with the build toolchain's own strip and free of build-machine path strings; code and data sections are byte-identical to the earlier unstripped build, and it is rebuilt byte for byte from different directories by source-offer/build-hostapd.sh. The stripped file itself ran in the bounded smoke test on one Home Assistant Green on 2026-10-31.
